A test that has never failed proves nothing. Auditor notes: ["STRUCTURAL: T23 (apps/api/src/order-templates/dto/update-order-template.dto.spec.ts:19) does not fail on an assertion — the `await pipe.transform(...)` is unwrapped, so the BadRequestException thrown by the pipe escapes the test body and the `expect(result.items[0])` on line 20 never runs. Verified failure header: `BadRequestException: Bad Request Exception ... at Object.<anonymous> (order-templates/dto/update-order-template.dto.spec.ts:19:20)`. Every sibling pin in the same file uses `await expect(...).rejects`, so this is an inconsistency, not a deliberate form.","BEHAVIORAL: T29 (update-recurring-invoice.dto.spec.ts:26) goes red on `expect(Dto).toBeDefined()` — it proves the DTO module is absent, not any validation behavior; its real oracle (`resolves.toEqual({notes:'x'})`) never executes. Unavoidable today (with metatype undefined the pipe is a pass-through and the resolves-assertion would pass vacuously), but the R24 oracle is currently unproven.","BEHAVIORAL: T22a (apps/mobile/__tests__/recurring-invoices-helpers.test.ts:70) expects `null` against the absent helper's `undefined` — the weakest possible discriminator between 'implemented and returns null' and 'not implemented'. T22b/T22c carry content-bearing oracles; all three receive the same `undefined`.","BEHAVIORAL: T13 (order-templates.pricing-and-items.spec.ts:208) goes red on `priceType` expected 'PROMO' received undefined; its distinguishing BOGO money oracles (promoFreeUnits 1, subtotal 20 vs today's 30, order subtotal 20) never execute because jest stops at the first failing assertion.","BEHAVIORAL: T14 (pricing-and-items.spec.ts:230) goes red on `resolveBuyerLinePrice ... toHaveBeenCalledWith` with 0 calls; the boxed-money oracles (unitPrice 20, subtotal 40 — the point of R9) never execute.","BEHAVIORAL: T16 (pricing-and-items.spec.ts:269) goes red on `priceType` expected 'STANDARD' received undefined. Its money half was deliberately moved to a pin in order-templates.service.spec.ts that already passes, so nothing in the red set distinguishes T16's fixture from T9/T15 today.","BEHAVIORAL: T25 (pricing-and-items.spec.ts:300) and T31 (recurring-invoices.schedule-outcome.spec.ts:221) both go red on `tenantTransaction toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1)` received 0; the deeper R21/R25 oracles (deleteMany-before-update ordering, `tenantId: \"test-tenant\"` on the nested creates) never execute.","BEHAVIORAL: T9's order-level oracles (tax 1.6, total 17.6) and T5's `getHours() === 0` midnight assertion never execute — both fail on an earlier assertion in the same body.","BEHAVIORAL: T24's pins in update-order-template.dto.spec.ts ('rejects qty 0', 'rejects a client-supplied unitPrice') pass today for a different reason than they will after the fix — today ANY `items` key is rejected as non-whitelisted, so they discriminate nothing. Same class of issue for the T30 pin 'accepts a full create-shaped body' in update-recurring-invoice.dto.spec.ts, which passes only because metatype undefined makes the pipe a pass-through."]. Per-test outcomes: [{"test":"REG-B46 T1 — next occurrence strictly after `from` (apps/api/src/recurring-invoices/recurring-invoices.schedule-outcome.spec.ts:62)","outcome":"assertion-failure","note":"Expected getMonth() 7, received 6. Own calendar oracle; matches plan §6."},{"test":"REG-B46 T3 — December rolls into January (schedule-outcome.spec.ts:76)","outcome":"assertion-failure","note":"Expected 2027, received 2026. Distinct oracle."},{"test":"REG-B46 T5 — time-of-day treated as its calendar day (schedule-outcome.spec.ts:83)","outcome":"assertion-failure","note":"Expected month 7, received 6. The getHours()===0 half never runs (fail-fast)."},{"test":"REG-B46 T6 — twelve consecutive cycles strictly advance (schedule-outcome.spec.ts:91)","outcome":"assertion-failure","note":"toBeGreaterThan on cycle 1: next.getTime() equals current.getTime(). Strongest invariant oracle in the set."},{"test":"REG-B46 T7 — claim carries the strictly-future nextRunAt (schedule-outcome.spec.ts:119)","outcome":"assertion-failure","note":"claimCall.data.nextRunAt month expected 7, received 6 — read from the argument the service actually passed."},{"test":"REG-B106 T17 — create failure restores nextRunAt, records FAILED, rethrows (schedule-outcome.spec.ts:137)","outcome":"assertion-failure","note":"recurringInvoice.update toHaveBeenCalledWith(...) with 0 calls. The rejects.toBe(failure) half already holds today; the FAILED-write shape is the new behavior."},{"test":"REG-B106 T18 — SUCCESS recorded only after create+link (schedule-outcome.spec.ts:160)","outcome":"assertion-failure","note":"calls expected [claim,create,link,status:SUCCESS], received [claim,create,link]. The log is built in the test's own mockImplementations but records production call order — a legitimate ordering oracle."},{"test":"REG-B106 T19 — claim stamps a provisional FAILED (schedule-outcome.spec.ts:188)","outcome":"assertion-failure","note":"claimCall.data.lastRunStatus expected 'FAILED', received undefined."},{"test":"REG-B92 T31 — recurring item replace inside one tenantTransaction (schedule-outcome.spec.ts:205)","outcome":"assertion-failure","note":"tenantTransaction toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1) received 0. I checked apps/api/src/testing/prisma-mock.ts:223 — tenantTransaction runs its callback against the same model mocks, so the inner deleteMany/update assertions are satisfiable after implementation."},{"test":"REG-B48 T9 — tier ladder tier2 -> priceTier2 + subtotal (apps/api/src/order-templates/order-templates.pricing-and-items.spec.ts:90)","outcome":"assertion-failure","note":"unitPrice expected 8, received 10. Runs the real OrdersService.prototype.resolveBuyerLinePrice, so the money value is arithmetic, not a mock mirror."},{"test":"REG-B48 T10 — CustomerPrice override beats the default tier (pricing-and-items.spec.ts:119)","outcome":"assertion-failure","note":"Expected 7, received 10. Distinct hand-derived value."},{"test":"REG-B48 T11 — null override falls through to the default tier (pricing-and-items.spec.ts:145)","outcome":"assertion-failure","note":"Expected 8, received 10. Distinct value."},{"test":"REG-B48 T12 — best promotion loaded for the CUSTOMER role (pricing-and-items.spec.ts:165)","outcome":"assertion-failure","note":"Expected 9, received 10. The loadActivePromotions('CUSTOMER') interaction oracle never runs (fail-fast), but the money value drives the red."},{"test":"REG-B48 T13 — BUY_N_GET_M reduces subtotal by whole free units (pricing-and-items.spec.ts:194)","outcome":"assertion-failure","note":"Fails on priceType expected 'PROMO' received undefined; the BOGO money oracles never execute. See BEHAVIORAL."},{"test":"REG-B48 T14 — boxed qty bills as whole boxes (pricing-and-items.spec.ts:215)","outcome":"assertion-failure","note":"resolveBuyerLinePrice toHaveBeenCalledWith(...) with 0 calls. Asserts on a jest.fn the test configured, but that fn wraps the REAL resolver and the assertion is about production calling it — acceptable; the money oracles behind it never execute."},{"test":"REG-B48 T15 — sticky upsell wins over the tier (pricing-and-items.spec.ts:240)","outcome":"assertion-failure","note":"Expected 12, received 10. Distinct hand-derived value."},{"test":"REG-B48 T16 — STANDARD + null originalPrice persisted (pricing-and-items.spec.ts:259)","outcome":"assertion-failure","note":"Expected 'STANDARD', received undefined. Money half parked in a pin that passes today. See BEHAVIORAL."},{"test":"REG-B48 T25 — update() replaces items atomically, deleteMany first (pricing-and-items.spec.ts:273)","outcome":"assertion-failure","note":"tenantTransaction toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1) received 0; tenantId-stamping oracle unexecuted."},{"test":"REG-B48 T26 — update() validates products before writing anything (pricing-and-items.spec.ts:313)","outcome":"assertion-failure","note":"rejects.toBeInstanceOf(BadRequestException) — received a resolved value {}. Genuine negative oracle."},{"test":"REG-B48 T23 — accepts items on a PATCH (apps/api/src/order-templates/dto/update-order-template.dto.spec.ts:18)","outcome":"error","note":"STRUCTURAL BLOCKER. The BadRequestException from pipe.transform escapes the unwrapped await on line 19; the assertion on line 20 never runs. The exception does come from the subject under test and does demonstrate the defect (items is non-whitelisted today), so the test is not mis-wired — but it fails on a thrown exception, not an assertion, and would fail identically for any unrelated pipe error. Remediation given."},{"test":"REG-B92 T29 — a partial body validates against the DTO class (apps/api/src/recurring-invoices/dto/update-recurring-invoice.dto.spec.ts:25)","outcome":"assertion-failure","note":"expect(Dto).toBeDefined() received undefined — the dynamic require/try-catch keeps this an assertion rather than a module-not-found error, as the plan intended. But it proves module absence, not behavior. See BEHAVIORAL."},{"test":"T22a — no last run / no status -> null (apps/mobile/__tests__/recurring-invoices-helpers.test.ts:70)","outcome":"assertion-failure","note":"toEqual(null) received undefined (jest does distinguish these at top level — verified by running it). Selected by the gate through the enclosing describe(\"REG-B106 lastRunOutcome\"); the it() titles carry no token themselves."},{"test":"T22b — FAILED run -> red pill with detail (recurring-invoices-helpers.test.ts:77)","outcome":"assertion-failure","note":"Expected {variant:'red',label:'Last run failed',detail:'Customer not found'}, received undefined. Own content-bearing expected value."},{"test":"T22c — SUCCESS run -> green pill (recurring-invoices-helpers.test.ts:89)","outcome":"assertion-failure","note":"Expected {variant:'green',label:'Last run succeeded'}, received undefined. Own expected value."},{"test":"PINS (untokened, outside the gate) — 4 cases in update-order-template.dto.spec.ts:25-43","outcome":"passed","note":"Pass because the pinned behavior already exists (rule-5 case 2), not because the assertions are vacuous — but two of them currently pass only because the whole items key is rejected as non-whitelisted, so they discriminate nothing today. Filtered out of the `-t \"REG-B\"` gate run by design; in my unfiltered run they executed and passed."},{"test":"PINS — the three T30 'rejects' cases in update-recurring-invoice.dto.spec.ts:30-42","outcome":"assertion-failure","note":"These currently FAIL (rejects... received resolved) because metatype is undefined and the ValidationPipe is a pass-through — exactly as test-plan §2 T30 predicted. Untokened, so outside the gate; they go green when the DTO lands. Consequence: `npx jest src/recurring-invoices` is red beyond the red set (24 failures unfiltered vs 21 in the gate)."},{"test":"PIN — T30 'accepts a full create-shaped body' (update-recurring-invoice.dto.spec.ts:44)","outcome":"passed","note":"Vacuous today: with metatype undefined the pipe accepts everything. Becomes meaningful only once the DTO exists."},{"test":"PINS appended to existing files — recurring-invoices.service.spec.ts (T2, T4, T8 x3, T20 extension, T21) and order-templates.service.spec.ts (T16 money half, T27)","outcome":"passed","note":"All pass in my unfiltered run (both suites green: 14/14 and 14/14). Characterization pins the plan places outside the gate. The one rewritten assertion (service.spec.ts:197-205, nextRunWrites filter replacing not.toHaveBeenCalled()) is disclosed in test-plan §2.2 and still passes today."}]. Remediation asked for: One edit, in apps/api/src/order-templates/dto/update-order-template.dto.spec.ts, lines 18-21. Replace:

  it("REG-B48 accepts items on a PATCH and whitelists productId/qty (T23)", async () => {
    const result = await pipe.transform({ name: "x", items: [{ productId: "p1", qty: 2 }] }, meta);
    expect(result.items[0]).toMatchObject({ productId: "p1", qty: 2 });
  });

with:

  it("REG-B48 accepts items on a PATCH and whitelists productId/qty (T23)", async () => {
    await expect(
      pipe.transform({ name: "x", items: [{ productId: "p1", qty: 2 }] }, meta),
    ).resolves.toMatchObject({ name: "x", items: [{ productId: "p1", qty: 2 }] });
  });

That makes the failure an assertion ("Received promise rejected instead of resolved"), matches the plan's §6 expected failure for T23 (`resolves … received rejection 400`), matches the form used by the four pins directly below it, and keeps the identical post-fix oracle (items survives whitelisting with productId/qty intact). Re-run `cd apps/api && npx jest src/order-templates/dto/update-order-template.dto.spec.ts -t "REG-B"` and confirm the failure block names the expectation instead of printing a bare BadRequestException. No other edits are needed — the remaining 23 red-set tests already fail on assertions.
